{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:102714","published":"2026-11-25T06:07:23.377438Z","modified":"2026-11-25T06:30:03.303520170Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-110264","CVE-2026-132825","CVE-2026-93577","CVE-2026-97229"],"summary":"Critical: ruby4.0 security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"Ruby is the interpreted scripting language for quick and easy object-oriented programming.  It has many features to process text files and to do system management tasks (as in Perl).  It is simple, straight-forward, and extensible.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* ruby: integer overflow issue in regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-93577)\n\n* ruby: integer overflow issue in CI/CD regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-97229)\n\n* ruby: integer overflow issue in regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-110264)\n\n* ruby: ruby: Heap-based buffer overflow via string case conversion (CVE-2026-132825)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* ruby4.0: Rebase to the latest Ruby 4.0 release [rhel-10] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-260673)\n\n* ruby4.0: Rebase to the latest Ruby 4.0 release [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-312591)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ruby4.0-rubygem-pg-debuginfo","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/ruby4.0-rubygem-pg-debuginfo?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:1.6.3-39.el10_3"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:102714.json"}},{"package":{"name":"ruby4.0-debugsource","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/ruby4.0-debugsource?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.0.10-39.el10_3"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repo